na reproved her for entertaining towards himself feelings so unbecoming a mother as he considered her. But when he was told that he was not her son, but of Viṣṇu and was cast into the sea by Śambara, he became enraged, and, challenging him to fight, succeeded in killing him by the force of illusions. He and Māyāvatī afterwards repaired to the house of Kṛiṣṇa, where Nārada told him and Rukmiṇī that the boy was their own and that Māyāvatī was his wife.]"}]}]}],"pradyumnakaH":[{"id":"pradyumnakaH","headword":"प्रद्युम्नकः","headword_slp1":"pradyumnakaH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रद्युम्नकः [pradyumnakḥ], N. of the god of love; Bhāg."}]}]}],"pradyotaH":[{"id":"pradyotaH","headword":"प्रद्योतः","headword_slp1":"pradyotaH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रद्योतः [pradyōtḥ], 1 Irradiating, lighting, illuminating."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Splendour, light, lustre."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"A ray of light."}]},{"n":4,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of a king of Ujjayinī, whose daughter Vatsa married; प्रद्योतस्य प्रियदुहितरं वत्सराजो$त्र जह्रे "},{"t":"cite","s":"Me.32","q":"Me"},{"t":"txt","s":". (considered as an interpolation by Malli.); "},{"t":"cite","s":"Ratn.1.1","q":"Ratn"},{"t":"txt","s":"."}]}]}],"pradyotanam":[{"id":"pradyotanam","headword":"प्रद्योतनम्","headword_slp1":"pradyotanam","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रद्योतनम् [pradyōtanam], 1 Blazing, shining."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"Light."}]},{"n":3,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"नः The sun."}]},{"n":4,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"N. of a prince of Ujjayinī."}]}]}],"pradrava":[{"id":"pradrava","headword":"प्रद्रव","headword_slp1":"pradrava","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रद्रव [pradrava], a. Fluid, liquid. -वः Running."}]}]}],"pradravaH":[{"id":"pradrAvaH","headword":"प्रद्रावः","headword_slp1":"pradrAvaH","senses_r":[{"n":1,"spans":[{"t":"txt","s":"प्रद्रावः [pradrāvḥ], 1 Running away, flight, retreat, escape."}]},{"n":2,"spans":[{